{"content_hash": "0e8fba318f41a6ba", "version_id": 637, "article_id": 64, "level_code": "ja_n4", "lang": "ja", "level": 2, "level_label": "N4 初級", "title": "スーダン国境で金をさがす人々が空爆で死亡", "title_zh": "苏丹边境淘金者遭空袭身亡", "has_translation": true, "topic": "world", "source": "bbc_world", "source_url": "https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cqy43vrk8wv8o?at_medium=RSS&at_campaign=rss", "image": {"type": "photo", "url": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1621837593522-eae4fc6a9f17?ixid=M3wxMDk3Mzk1fDB8MXxzZWFyY2h8N3x8ZG96ZW5zJTIwZ29sZCUyMHByb3NwZWN0b3JzfGVufDB8MHx8fDE3OTE3NjYxMzJ8MA&ixlib=rb-4.1.0&w=1600&q=75&fm=jpg&fit=max", "provider": "unsplash", "credit": "Photo by Kanchanara on Unsplash", "author": "Kanchanara", "credit_url": "https://unsplash.com/@kanchanara?utm_source=daily-english-news&utm_medium=referral", "source": "Unsplash", "source_url": "https://unsplash.com/photos/silver-and-black-round-pendant-necklace-tayj2w_LCHI?utm_source=daily-english-news&utm_medium=referral", "fallback": {"type": "gradient", "from": "hsl(69, 42%, 62%)", "to": "hsl(107, 46%, 48%)", "label": "WORLD", "seed": "8fb5b734dbc5"}}, "published_date": "2026-10-12", "word_count": 168, "reading_minutes": 0.5, "lead": "スーダンとエジプトの国境近くで、金をさがしていた人たちが空爆されました。人権団体によると、少なくとも72人が亡くなりました。", "lead_zh": "在苏丹与埃及边境附近，正在淘金的人们遭到空袭。据人权组织称，至少72人死亡。", "preview": "スーダンの首都ハルタムにある人権団体「エマージェンシー・ローヤーズ」が発表しました。土曜日、スーダン北部のナイル川州にある金鉱山で、飛行機が市民を攻撃したということです。エジプト政府もスーダン当局も、まだ何も言っていません。", "preview_zh": "位于苏丹首都喀土穆的人权组织“紧急律师”发布了消息。据称，周六在苏丹北部尼罗河州的一处金矿，飞机袭击了平民。埃及政府和苏丹当局目前都未发表任何言论。", "has_audio": true, "audio": {"id": 625, "url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/audio/64/ja_n4.mp3", "duration": 32.65, "size_bytes": 199584, "engine": "edge-tts", "voice": "ja-JP-NanamiNeural", "word_count": 101, "has_timeline": true}, "detail_url": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/chjam12301-sys/news-etl@0c12f88/content/data/versions/637.json", "paragraphs": ["スーダンの首都ハルタムにある人権団体「エマージェンシー・ローヤーズ」が発表しました。土曜日、スーダン北部のナイル川州にある金鉱山で、飛行機が市民を攻撃したということです。エジプト政府もスーダン当局も、まだ何も言っていません。", "この団体は「武器を持たない市民をわざと攻撃するのは戦争犯罪になる可能性がある」と言いました。亡くなった人の数はまだ増えるかもしれません。"], "paragraphs_zh": ["位于苏丹首都喀土穆的人权组织“紧急律师”发布了消息。据称，周六在苏丹北部尼罗河州的一处金矿，飞机袭击了平民。埃及政府和苏丹当局目前都未发表任何言论。", "该组织表示：“故意攻击手无寸铁的平民可能构成战争罪。”死亡人数可能还会增加。"], "body": "スーダンの首都ハルタムにある人権団体「エマージェンシー・ローヤーズ」が発表しました。土曜日、スーダン北部のナイル川州にある金鉱山で、飛行機が市民を攻撃したということです。エジプト政府もスーダン当局も、まだ何も言っていません。\n\nこの団体は「武器を持たない市民をわざと攻撃するのは戦争犯罪になる可能性がある」と言いました。亡くなった人の数はまだ増えるかもしれません。", "body_zh": "位于苏丹首都喀土穆的人权组织“紧急律师”发布了消息。据称，周六在苏丹北部尼罗河州的一处金矿，飞机袭击了平民。埃及政府和苏丹当局目前都未发表任何言论。\n\n该组织表示：“故意攻击手无寸铁的平民可能构成战争罪。”死亡人数可能还会增加。", "text": "スーダンの首都ハルタムにある人権団体「エマージェンシー・ローヤーズ」が発表しました。土曜日、スーダン北部のナイル川州にある金鉱山で、飛行機が市民を攻撃したということです。エジプト政府もスーダン当局も、まだ何も言っていません。 この団体は「武器を持たない市民をわざと攻撃するのは戦争犯罪になる可能性がある」と言いました。亡くなった人の数はまだ増えるかもしれません。", "vocab": [{"word": "空爆", "pos": "noun", "zh": "空袭", "note": "从飞机上进行的轰炸", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "国境", "pos": "noun", "zh": "边境", "note": "国家之间的边界", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "人権団体", "pos": "noun", "zh": "人权组织", "note": "保护人权的团体", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "市民", "pos": "noun", "zh": "市民，平民", "note": "普通居民", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "攻撃", "pos": "noun/verb", "zh": "攻击", "note": "用武力打击", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "戦争犯罪", "pos": "noun", "zh": "战争罪", "note": "违反战争规则的罪行", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "生き残った", "pos": "verb", "zh": "幸存下来的", "note": "在危险中活下来", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "内戦", "pos": "noun", "zh": "内战", "note": "国内不同集团之间的战争", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "許可", "pos": "noun", "zh": "许可", "note": "得到允许", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "押収", "pos": "noun/verb", "zh": "没收，查获", "note": "官方扣押物品", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}], "title_original": "Dozens of gold prospectors killed in strikes on Egypt-Sudan border, rights group says", "summary_original": "Neither Egypt nor Sudan has commented on the alleged strikes on an artisanal mining camp on Saturday.", "body_original": "Dozens of gold prospectors killed in strikes on Egypt-Sudan border, rights group says\nBy\nAleks Phillips\nPublished\n3 hours ago\nAt least 72 civilians who had been prospecting for gold in a border region of Sudan have been killed in air strikes, a regional rights group says.\nEmergency Lawyers, based in the Sudanese capital, Khartoum, said jets targeted the so-called artisanal miners at a popular gold mining sites in Sudan's River Nile state on Saturday.\nNeither the Egyptian government nor the de facto Sudanese authorities have so far commented.\nCairo has previously faced accusations of deadly strikes on gold prospectors as part of a crackdown on illicit activity along its southern border.\nEmergency Lawyers noted the previous alleged attacks and said they represented not only a violation of Sudan's sovereign territory but demonstrated the government's lack of control over the region.\n\"The deliberate targeting of unarmed civilians violates international humanitarian law and the right to life,\" it said in a statement on Sunday. \"These acts may constitute war crimes.\"\nIt noted that its death toll was provisional and could rise.\nThe Paris-based Sudan Tribune reported that the death toll could far exceed the number reported by Emergency Lawyers, citing a survivor of Saturday's attack who said many more people had been injured.\nEyewitnesses said the attack began around 06:00 local time (04:00 GMT), with the aircraft firing more than five missiles directly at the miners' camps, destroying them and excavation pits with people still inside, the newspaper wrote.\nThe Sudan Tribune reported claims in June that Egyptian forces had used drones and artillery to target artisanal mining sites in the same region, killing several, after sporadic incidents of Egyptian border guards of burning equipment, torching temporary shelters, and firing live ammunition to disperse mine workers.\nDays later, Egypt's border agency announced that it and the military had begun a sweeping security campaign along the border to foil illegal migration, drug smuggling and illegal mining.\nAt the same time, Sudan's de facto leader announced an investigation into the alleged strikes, which were said to have killed dozens.\nGold lies at the core of the border tensions.\nSudan's ongoing civil war has led to a surge in artisanal mining - an often risky practice conducted by civilians with rudimentary tools and without official permission - particularly in remote areas near its borders.\nGold-rich areas such as those in River Nile state lie along porous borders in terrain historically associated with cross-border smuggling routes, with artisanally mined gold potentially feeding into those channels.\nEgypt's border force said in June that it had seized 86 tonnes of gold ore along with amateur prospecting equipment.\nArtisanal mining has also reportedly continued in Sudan's conflict zones and smuggled gold may be a source of income for armed insurgent groups.\nThis has raised concerns of illicit Sudanese gold undermining the legitimate Egyptian gold market.\nRelated topics\nSudan\nEgypt\nAfrica\nMining\nMore on this story\nA simple guide to what is happening in Sudan\nPublished\n13 November 2025", "fetched_at": "2026-10-12T00:48:50.607058", "timeline": [{"i": 0, "w": "スーダン", "s": 0.125, "e": 0.637, "sm": 125, "em": 637, "cs": 0, "ce": 4, "si": 0}, {"i": 1, "w": "の", "s": 0.65, "e": 0.775, "sm": 650, "em": 775, "cs": 4, "ce": 5, "si": 0}, {"i": 2, "w": "首都", "s": 0.787, "e": 1.025, "sm": 787, "em": 1025, "cs": 5, "ce": 7, "si": 0}, {"i": 3, "w": "ハルタム", "s": 1.038, "e": 1.488, "sm": 1037, "em": 1487, "cs": 7, "ce": 11, "si": 0}, {"i": 4, "w": "に", "s": 1.5, "e": 1.613, "sm": 1500, "em": 1612, "cs": 11, "ce": 12, "si": 0}, {"i": 5, "w": "ある", "s": 1.625, "e": 1.863, "sm": 1625, "em": 1862, "cs": 12, "ce": 14, "si": 0}, {"i": 6, "w": "人権", "s": 1.875, "e": 2.337, "sm": 1875, "em": 2337, "cs": 14, "ce": 16, "si": 0}, {"i": 7, "w": "団体", "s": 2.35, "e": 2.837, "sm": 2350, "em": 2837, "cs": 16, "ce": 18, "si": 0}, {"i": 8, "w": "「", "s